      "text": "Kinematic equations for constant acceleration relate an object's position, velocity, and acceleration when the acceleration does not change over time.",
      "sources": [
        "S7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Newton stated his second law in terms of momentum, indicating that the instantaneous rate at which a body's momentum changes is equal to the net force acting on the body.",
      "sources": [
        "S2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This relationship is given by the vector equation $\\vec{F}_{net} = \\frac{d\\vec{p}}{dt}$.",
      "sources": [
        "S1",
        "S2",
        "S3",
        "S6"
      ]
    }
  ],
