      "text": "In free-fall motion, where air resistance and friction are negligible, all objects fall with the same constant acceleration toward the center of Earth, independent of their mass.",
      "sources": [
        "S1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Although people once believed that heavier objects have greater acceleration, heavy objects and lighter objects actually arrive at the ground at the same time when dropped from the same height.",
      "sources": [
        "S1"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "missing": "",
  "outside": "",
  "check_question": "If you drop a heavy rock and a light plastic ball in a vacuum where there is no air resistance, which one hits the ground first?",
